 runtime assertions","messageBody":"Jeremy needs a graphical interface for users to interact with\ntask commands more conveniently. Important assumptions about\ninputs, task construction, storage, and GUI initialization should\nalso be documented in executable form.\n\nLet\u0027s:\n* connect the JavaFX interface to Jeremy\u0027s command processing\n* support adding, listing, finding, marking, unmarking, and deleting tasks\n* persist task changes through the existing storage component\n* add assertions for important object and input assumptions\n* enable assertions when running the application through Gradle\n\nThis preserves the existing console functionality while allowing\nthe GUI and command-line interface to share the same task logic.\n","tags":["A-FullCommitMessage","A-Assertions"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":5,"deletions":0},"java":{"insertions":25,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"5cbf5d69112ab4adaf65a9fdc7b7e1cfaa1f0810","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Jeremy: simplify JavaFX layout setup","messageBody":"Jeremy\u0027s JavaFX setup contains several layout responsibilities and unexplained numeric values in one method.\n\nExtract the setup responsibilities into focused helper methods and replace layout literals with named constants.\n\nThis improves readability and makes future GUI changes easier without changing behaviour.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":32,"deletions":15}}},{"hash":"8592cbbf1ba39ffabd2d4281ba2bb6a1428047a9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"TaskList: protect internal task storage","messageBody":"TaskList exposes its mutable internal list through asList(), allowing callers to modify task storage directly.\n\nReturn a read-only view instead.\n\nThis preserves encapsulation and ensures task mutations remain controlled by TaskList\u0027s public operations.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":6,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"caff1262113fe8dee044c41da57fb8e84d7e0d7b","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add assertions for runtime assumptions","messageBody":"Important assumptions about command inputs, task construction, storage, and GUI initialization are implicit in the code.\n\nAdd Java assert statements to document these assumptions and enable assertions during Gradle runs.\n\nThis makes violated internal assumptions visible during development without replacing the existing JUnit tests.\n","tags":["A-CodeQuality"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":12,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"7244d1abd605a3883f2d611f806d51f88e7b0584","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into branch-A-CodeQuality","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-09-10T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"4e8d9e9c85c065579781f0dcb40fdba6d762ff18","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #1 from AAAchinnn/branch-A-CodeQuality","messageBody":"Improvements in Code Quality","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]}]},"authorFileTypeContributionMap":{"AAAchinnn":{"java":1150,"md":0,"fxml":0,"sh":0,"bat":93,"gradle":61,"txt":0}},"authorContributionVariance":{"AAAchinnn":120904.8},"authorDisplayNameMap":{"AAAchinnn":"CS2103T-T08-2 ACHI..ASAN"}}
